<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Küchük Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1459</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Küchük Muhammad was a khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> in the mid 15th century, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarai">Sarai</a> as the Horde broke apart. His rump state, known as the Great Horde, claimed seniority among the Jochid successor states. His sons continued to rule the Great Horde, and his descendants founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan-khanate">Astrakhan Khanate</a> in the 1460s.</p></div>
